From 2a02cf6c4797f615e8e687954b913e332f007158 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oleksandr Kostenko <sanyokkua@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 10:07:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] macOS: Settings window (Cmd+,) and Resolution Scale on Metal

NFS Underground > Settings... in the menu bar SDL makes (Quit is Cmd+Q
there): Display (window / full screen, now and at start), Frame Rate (60 or
the original 30, at the next start) and Resolution Scale (1x..2.5x, now).
Display and Frame Rate are kept in settings.ini in the working directory
and become NFSU2_FULLSCREEN / NFSU2_FPS_CAP defaults; set variables win.

Options > Camera > Resolution Scale, Vulkan-only before, now also on Metal
(nv2a_metal.m rescales at the next flip); the window and the row share the
value and nfsu1x_options.txt. Default 1.5x (was 1x on Metal).
